    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1 · Completion trigger\nFolder **02_completed_snapshots**. The filename convention `TICKET-<id>.jpg` links the AFTER photo to its ticket.\nUnmatched files or invalid/closed tickets → FM alert (no silent dead ends).",
        "width": 400,
        "height": 220,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "616a8564-b9e2-41c0-bc50-2982d35e18d7",
      "name": "Sticky - Completion",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1280,
        120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2 · AI before/after verification\nBEFORE photo is re-downloaded from the ticket record, AFTER comes from the trigger; the two binaries are merged into one item.\nClaude compares them and stores a JSON verdict. This is a **pre-screen for the FM, not a decision** — the FM keeps final authority (hard constraint).",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 280,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "582150a9-a557-48af-8ed5-c8f361843384",
      "name": "Sticky - Verify",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -360,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3 · FM gate → IFC update → closure\nOnly an explicit FM approval closes the ticket and writes the maintenance Pset into the IFC (a **new version file**; the model is never overwritten).\nIf the IFC service is down the ticket still closes with `ifc_version = IFC_SYNC_FAILED` for a later re-sync.\nRejection → status REWORK → technician re-uploads with the same filename and this workflow re-triggers.\nAfter import, verify *Limit Wait Time* = 72 h on the FM approval node.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 320,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "12fc4583-2b09-4d47-af72-497392eda0ee",
      "name": "Sticky - Closure",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        800,
        60
      ]
    },
